# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Aim Universe - development repository exclusions (BASE-02)
#
# The point of this file: the maintainable source can be versioned, while the
# restricted business payload never can. Ignore rules are a supplement to
# keeping restricted data in the authorised local area - not a security control.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Restricted: the extracted embedded business payload (pilot accounts, supplier
# purchase-cost series). Regenerable locally from the authorised v03 artifact.
payload/*.json
!payload/*.synthetic.json

# Restricted: the frozen v03 reproduction reference embeds both pilots and the
# supplier cost table. It stays on disk as a reference and out of version control.
reference/*.html
reference/*.htm

# Generated internal artifact (embeds the restricted payload when built from it)
dist/*.html
dist/*.cmd

# Local QA output
_qa/
_qa/**
**/_qa/**

# Test run output. These are regenerated on every run, and they are NOT safe to
# version: the checks that run against the real payload echo scenario fields into
# their result files, which include the restricted parts purchase cost. Measured:
# accept_01_engine.json, accept_02_journey.json and accept_04_participant.json
# each carry a cost value. 277 output files were reachable before this rule.
tests/accept/_out/**
tests/**/_out/**
test-results/
*.test.log

# Local baseline captures from an authorised payload run
_baseline_real.json

# Tool noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
.tmp/
*.tmp
*.log
